<p>These Connect Terms govern authorized business access to Koast's operator software, including dispatch and related administration tools, provided by Krujim Inc, doing business as Koast. "Operator" means the transportation company using the software; "you" means that company or an authorized user acting within their role. Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how personal information is handled.</p>

<h2 id="authority">1. Authority and scope</h2>
<p>Use Connect only with the authority of the company whose records you access. If you accept a business agreement for a company, you must have authority to bind it. A staff sign-in does not authorize that staff member to purchase a subscription, change another person's agreement or act outside their assigned permissions.</p>
<p>These terms address software access. A separately executed order form, subscription agreement or data-processing addendum may set additional commercial and processing terms. Chauffeurs using Driver are also covered by the <a href="/terms/driver/">Driver App Terms</a>. Passenger bookings are subject to the relevant transportation agreement; the <a href="/terms/rider/">Koast Rider Terms</a> apply where Koast provides or arranges the booking under those terms.</p>

<h2 id="operator-responsibilities">2. The operator's responsibilities</h2>
<p>The operator is responsible for its lawful transportation operation, required permits and insurance, chauffeur and vehicle eligibility, customer commitments, staff authorization, published prices and booking policies, tax treatment and support arrangements. Software availability is not certification that an operator, chauffeur or vehicle meets a regulatory requirement.</p>
<p>Maintain accurate records and review material actions, including dispatch assignments, service changes, invoices, charges and refunds. Use AI assistance as a tool; verify important output and use a human decision-maker for consequential operational or compliance decisions. Keep a manual communication and recovery process for outages and urgent rides.</p>

<h2 id="accounts">3. Accounts and access</h2>
<p>Assign accounts and permissions only to authorized people. Keep sign-in methods secure, remove access when it is no longer needed and report suspected misuse promptly. Do not share credentials, bypass organization boundaries or access records belonging to another company without authorization. Koast may apply security checks and restrict access to address credible security, safety or unlawful-use concerns, subject to applicable law and the governing business agreement.</p>

<h2 id="customer-records">4. Customer records and privacy responsibilities</h2>
<p>The operator retains its rights in its business records and operator-originated customer relationships. Koast processes records as needed to provide, secure and support the software, carry out authorized instructions and meet applicable obligations. Using Connect does not authorize Koast to use an operator's private customer list to market around that operator or to supply that list to another operator.</p>
<p>The operator must have a lawful basis for the information it uploads, the communications it requests and the permissions it grants. It must give appropriate customer and workforce notices and obtain required consent, including for optional recordings, device tracking and messaging. Acceptance of these terms is not a passenger's consent to those activities.</p>
<p>Operator customer records, private notes, ride and payment history and saved payment methods remain scoped to the relevant organization. A fulfilling operator and chauffeur receive the information needed for the particular reservation they perform. Future portable profile sharing across operators requires a separately explained rider choice before activation. It is not enabled or authorized by accepting these terms.</p>
<p>Coordinate privacy, access and deletion requests with Koast when software records are involved. Separately agreed data-processing provisions may further define instructions, safeguards, providers, incident handling and assistance. These public terms are not a substitute for any required data-processing agreement.</p>

<h2 id="commercial">5. Subscriptions, charges and third-party services</h2>
<p>Any paid plan, subscription term, renewal, cancellation process, usage charge or network fee must be stated in the applicable order form, subscription agreement or purchase flow accepted by an authorized company representative. These terms do not establish a new price, minimum term or automatic renewal on their own. Staff sign-in is not an authorization to charge a company or a customer.</p>
<p>Configure and use payment features only with proper authorization and an agreed basis for each charge. The relevant payment-provider agreement and reservation terms also apply. Software access does not activate a payment-splitting arrangement, establish a merchant of record for every ride, or authorize transfers between companies.</p>
<p>Optional third-party integrations are subject to their availability, permissions and applicable terms. Disconnect integrations when no longer authorized. Koast may change an integration as needed for security or provider changes, subject to the applicable business agreement.</p>

<h2 id="network">6. Affiliates and fulfillment</h2>
<p>Using Connect alone does not enroll the operator in an exclusive network or authorize another company to fulfill a reservation. Any affiliate or distributed-fulfillment arrangement must identify the customer owner, service brand, fulfilling operator, payment responsibility, support owner and commercial terms. The relevant parties must agree to those arrangements before relying on them. These terms do not activate a planned network feature.</p>

<h2 id="rights-use">7. Software rights and acceptable use</h2>
<p>Koast permits authorized use of the software for the agreed business purpose while access remains available. Koast and its licensors retain their software and branding rights. The operator retains its rights in content it lawfully supplies and permits processing needed to provide, secure and support the agreed service.</p>
<p>Do not introduce malicious code, interfere with the service, scrape restricted records, attempt unauthorized access, impersonate another user or use the platform for unlawful, abusive or fraudulent activity. Do not use another company's data to compete with it without its authorization.</p>

<h2 id="ending-access">8. Changes, outages and ending access</h2>
<p>Service functions may change, and internet, device or provider failures may affect availability. Any contractual uptime commitment, service credit, support tier, liability allocation or business offboarding arrangement is specified in the governing business agreement.</p>
<p>When access ends, coordinate outstanding services, authorized record access and offboarding with Koast and the operator's administrator. Do not assume deleting a user account cancels a subscription, deletes company records or cancels a passenger reservation. Privacy requests and lawful retention obligations are handled as described in the Privacy Policy and any applicable data-processing agreement.</p>

<h2 id="updates-contact">9. Updates, agreement order and contact</h2>
<p>We identify revisions by date and provide notice of material changes where required. A separately executed business agreement governing the same subject controls to the extent of a conflict, subject to applicable law. These public access terms do not introduce a separate arbitration requirement, liability cap, indemnity or waiver of mandatory rights.</p>
